WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:04.890
As the star of one of the most long-lived
superhero film franchises, Hugh Jackman has

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:10.500
been contractually obligated to keep his body
in a near-constant state of shreddedness since

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:11.750
1999.

00:00:11.750 --> 00:00:15.300
That's just how it goes when you're famous
for playing a character whose costume often

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:19.540
consists of one pair of adamantium claws and
a veiny pair of pecs.

00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:25.740
But how did Jackman transform from a 6-foot-2,
180-pound beanpole into the musclebound Wolverine?

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:30.340
Here's everything that goes into making, and
maintaining, his incredible physique.

00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:32.279
He never skips the gym

00:00:32.279 --> 00:00:36.739
If you've been watching Jackman play Wolverine
since the very beginning, you might have noticed

00:00:36.739 --> 00:00:40.239
that he hasn't just kept himself in terrific
shape — he's clearly set out to make each

00:00:40.239 --> 00:00:43.899
of his appearances even more physically intimidating
than the last.

00:00:43.899 --> 00:00:49.170
When Jackman first showed up in 2000's X-Men,
he looked good... but in an achievable way,

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:52.940
like your friend from work who goes to the
gym in the morning and only drinks light beer.

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:58.109
Celebrity trainer David Kingsbury revealed
Jackman's formula for success, and it involves

00:00:58.109 --> 00:01:01.059
going to the gym six days a week, twice a
day.

00:01:01.059 --> 00:01:06.300
The actor follows a four-week workout cycle
when he's planning to slip back into his adamantium-laced

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:07.300
bones.

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:11.280
The first three weeks are all about lifting
heavy, and pushing huge amount of weight for

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:12.910
only a few repetitions.

00:01:12.910 --> 00:01:17.690
The fourth week, Jackman de-loads and lifts
smaller amounts but at a higher volume, which

00:01:17.690 --> 00:01:21.400
stimulates muscle growth so that he'll be
as big as possible on-screen.

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:23.750
The whole thing is pretty much murder on his
wardrobe.

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:29.270
"There boxes in my storage: fat suits, skinny
suits, and normal suits.

00:01:29.270 --> 00:01:33.830
And  um, right now, in this shape,
I don't have any suits."

00:01:33.830 --> 00:01:37.800
Jackman told the LA Times that there's one
thing that he favors above all when it comes

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:41.570
to transforming his body for a new X-Men movie:
the deadlift.

00:01:41.570 --> 00:01:43.780
And that's not just a clever pun.

00:01:43.780 --> 00:01:45.710
He eats all the food

00:01:45.710 --> 00:01:50.000
When it comes to building a screen-ready physique,
your workouts are less than half the battle.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:52.540
"You've got to train and you've got to train
hard.

00:01:52.540 --> 00:01:54.580
If you don't eat right, none of it matters."

00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:59.020
To get Wolverine-style muscles, Jackman has
to seriously shovel it in.

00:01:59.020 --> 00:02:00.070
Jackman told Men's Fitness,

00:02:00.070 --> 00:02:02.680
"I eat more, but I eat a lot stricter.

00:02:02.680 --> 00:02:07.320
Seventy percent of your physique is your diet,
and diet is the biggest change that happens.

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:11.819
There were times when I would literally eat
with the mindset of working out.

00:02:11.819 --> 00:02:14.480
'One more mouthful, one more, come on, come
on, you've got to finish this meal.'"

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:19.829
The actor's X-Men diet of 6,000 calories per
day was recommended by a guy who knows a thing

00:02:19.829 --> 00:02:21.760
or two about getting buff for a role.

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:24.540
"I literally rang Dwayne Johnson, 'The Rock.'"

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:25.540
"OK."

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:27.290
"I've seen you in some movies.

00:02:27.290 --> 00:02:28.290
What's going on?

00:02:28.290 --> 00:02:29.290
What do I do?"

00:02:29.290 --> 00:02:32.939
And before you go thinking that this doesn't
sound so terrible, keep in mind that Jackman's

00:02:32.939 --> 00:02:37.519
superhero diet is high in calories but low
in carbs, which means that he has to get those

00:02:37.519 --> 00:02:42.879
6,000 calories primarily in the form of grilled
chicken breast, spinach, and the occasional

00:02:42.879 --> 00:02:44.239
scoop of brown rice.

00:02:44.239 --> 00:02:49.299
...Though Jackman was seen celebrating with
some very un-diet-like foods after Logan finished

00:02:49.299 --> 00:02:50.480
filming.

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:52.859
He uses what nature gave him

00:02:52.859 --> 00:02:57.540
Before you spend the rest of your life weeping
into a bowl of buttered popcorn over the unattainable

00:02:57.540 --> 00:03:02.329
awesomeness of Hugh Jackman's abs, know that
getting a body like his isn't just a question

00:03:02.329 --> 00:03:06.040
of chicken breasts, bicep curls, and impeccable
genes.

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:10.109
Jackman's trainer explained that the actor's
diet and training regimen included the use

00:03:10.109 --> 00:03:14.659
of creatine, a supplement that stimulates
muscle growth beyond what the body can accomplish

00:03:14.659 --> 00:03:15.659
on its own.

00:03:15.659 --> 00:03:16.659
He explained,

00:03:16.659 --> 00:03:18.969
"We used a pre-workout product called Animal
Pump.

00:03:18.969 --> 00:03:24.209
While bulking, we used creatine in the product,
and when cutting, we reduced, and then removed

00:03:24.209 --> 00:03:25.209
the creatine."

00:03:25.209 --> 00:03:29.739
It's not exactly the Weapon X program — even
the strictest anti-doping regulators are cool

00:03:29.739 --> 00:03:33.879
with the use of creatine, and it's been a
regular item on the menu for bodybuilders

00:03:33.879 --> 00:03:36.499
and athletes since the 1990s.

00:03:36.499 --> 00:03:41.560
But it is one of the reasons why you don't
look like Wolverine despite your best efforts.

00:03:41.560 --> 00:03:43.389
Broadway bod

00:03:43.389 --> 00:03:47.049
Jackman is a stage actor first and foremost,
with a background on Broadway.

00:03:47.049 --> 00:03:51.060
He'd be the first to tell you that Wolverine,
for all his exceptional talents, would not

00:03:51.060 --> 00:03:52.309
be much of a dancer.

00:03:52.309 --> 00:03:56.559
So, the actor doesn't hang onto his superheroic
physique when he's doing shows in between

00:03:56.559 --> 00:03:57.859
superhero flicks.

00:03:57.859 --> 00:03:59.030
He told the LA Times,

00:03:59.030 --> 00:04:01.529
"[When] I dance I drop muscle very quickly.

00:04:01.529 --> 00:04:05.779
The body is very smart and efficient, and
a traditional dancer's body is not going to

00:04:05.779 --> 00:04:08.810
be bulked up on top because they're muscles
that you don't really need."

00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:13.590
While doing stage work may cost Jackman his
biceps, it also has the benefit of keeping

00:04:13.590 --> 00:04:15.059
Jackman in terrific shape.

00:04:15.059 --> 00:04:19.859
When the cameras stop rolling, the actor still
stays busy and active, and doesn't let himself

00:04:19.859 --> 00:04:20.859
go.

00:04:20.859 --> 00:04:25.060
So when it comes time to bulk up beserker-style,
he's starting from a very good place.

00:04:25.060 --> 00:04:26.729
He stays accountable

00:04:26.729 --> 00:04:31.530
Getting in superhero shape isn't just diet
and exercise — it's also a question of mindset

00:04:31.530 --> 00:04:32.590
and motivation.

00:04:32.590 --> 00:04:37.490
So, where does Jackman get the mental fortitude
to endure the months of torture that precede

00:04:37.490 --> 00:04:38.580
a new X-Men flick?

00:04:38.580 --> 00:04:39.990
He gets it from you, of course.

00:04:39.990 --> 00:04:43.760
Jackman always makes sure his followers know
when he's back in the gym, and that's not

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:46.509
just because he enjoys watching his Instagram
likes roll in.

00:04:46.509 --> 00:04:51.479
When you've taught your fans to expect photos
and videos of you doing clap pushups or deadlifting

00:04:51.479 --> 00:04:55.900
the weight of a fat Shetland pony, you've
gotta bring it at the gym or risk disappointing

00:04:55.900 --> 00:04:56.900
them.

00:04:56.900 --> 00:05:00.260
So when you follow Jackman on Instagram and
dutifully press that little heart icon for

00:05:00.260 --> 00:05:04.380
his clips from the gym, you're doing your
part to make sure he shows up in Logan looking

00:05:04.380 --> 00:05:07.199
like a muscular nest of pythons with a human
head.

00:05:07.199 --> 00:05:08.500
Thanks for watching!

00:05:08.500 --> 00:05:11.330
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:13.550
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

